                <pb facs="0570" n="458" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7460: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-01T09:00:00+08:00">December 1, 1935—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 1—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>121. Ho Ying-chin, appointed Executive Yuan representative in Peiping,
                    accompanied by Chen Yi, Provincial Chairman [of] Fukien, and Hsiung Shih-hui,
                    Provincial Chairman [of] Kiangsi, left Nanking by special train November 30, 10
                    p.m. for Peiping to deal with Sino-Japanese relations.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
